69}, {"candidate": "0xffadb0bba4379dfabfb20ca6823f6ec439429ec2", "detector_index": 170}, {"candidate": "0xffadb0bba4379dfabfb20ca6823f6ec439429ec2", "detector_index": 171}, {"candidate": "0xffadb0bba4379dfabfb20ca6823f6ec439429ec2", "detector_index": 172}, {"candidate": "0xffadb0bba4379dfabfb20ca6823f6ec439429ec2", "detector_index": 173}, {"candidate": "0xffadb0bba4379dfabfb20ca6823f6ec439429ec2", "detector_index": 174}, {"candidate": "0xffadb0bba4379dfabfb20ca6823f6ec439429ec2", "detector_index": 230}, {"candidate": "0xffadb0bba4379dfabfb20ca6823f6ec439429ec2", "detector_index": 231}, {"candidate": "0xffadb0bba4379dfabfb20ca6823f6ec439429ec2", "detector_index": 232}], "victim_has_source": true, "confidence": "medium", "notes": "With 1 WETH of collateral the attacker borrowed OHM (9 dec), USDC (6 dec) and WBTC (8 dec) worth about $1.4M, which only works if the price fed to the liquidity check was normalized inconsistently across token decimals; public write-ups describe a price-normalization/decimals error in the lending stack. The Comptroller candidate's math is stock Compound and the mis-scaled price comes from the external oracle, which is not among the recovered candidates, so the defect contract is not in the Slither set and no finding describes it. boolean-cst/boolean-equal and naming findings are Compound-style noise."}
{"incident_id": "20240309_UnizenIO", "reviewer": "fable-5.1 (blind LLM review)", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-22T12:57:23Z", "victim_addresses": ["0xd3f64baa732061f8b3626ee44bab354f854877ac"], "in_scope": true, "off_chain_reason": null, "root_cause": ["arbitrary_external_call", "input_validation"], "mechanism": ["crafted_calldata"], "impact": ["funds_drained"], "violated_invariant": "A contract that holds user token approvals must never execute caller-supplied calldata against a caller-chosen target, otherwise anyone can spend those approvals via transferFrom.", "locations": [{"raw": "TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol:_fallback", "role": "entry_point"}], "explains_findings": [], "valid_findings": [], "invalid_findings": [], "victim_has_source": false, "confidence": "high", "notes": "The PoC sends a crafted aggregator call whose embedded payload is DMTR.transferFrom(victim, aggregator, balance), so the aggregator implementation forwards attacker-chosen target+calldata and spends approvals users gave it. Only the OpenZeppelin proxy source was recovered; the implementation is unverified, so the defect function is not in the Slither set and every recovered finding is dependency-library noise about the proxy, not the exploit."}
{"incident_id": "20240430_PikeFinance", "reviewer": "fable-5.1 (blind LLM review)", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-22T12:57:23Z", "victim_addresses": ["0xfc7599cffea9de127a9f9c748ccb451a34d2f063"], "in_scope": true, "off_chain_reason": null, "root_cause": ["uninitialized_or_unprotected_init"], "mechanism": ["crafted_calldata"], "impact": ["funds_drained"], "violated_invariant": "initialize() on an upgradeable (UUPS) contract must be callable only once by the deployer, so ownership and the upgrade right can never be claimed by an outsider.", "locations": [{"raw": "(unrecovered implementation):initialize", "role": "defect"}, {"raw": "(unrecovered implementation):upgradeToAndCall", "role": "affected"}], "explains_findings": [], "valid_findings": [], "invalid_findings": [], "victim_has_source": false, "confidence": "high", "notes": "The PoC simply calls initialize() on the live proxy to become owner, then upgradeToAndCall to a malicious implementation that sends the ETH balance out, which is the classic unprotected initializer. No source was recovered for the proxy or implementation, so there are no Slither findings to adjudicate."}
{"incident_id": "20240705_DeFiPlaza", "reviewer": "fable-5.1 (blind LLM review)", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-22T12:57:23Z", "victim_addresses": ["0xe68c1d72340aeefe5be76eda63ae2f4bc7514110"], "in_scope": true, "off_chain_reason": null, "root_cause": ["rounding_precision", "business_logic"], "mechanism": ["flash_loan", "other"], "impact": ["funds_drained"], "violated_invariant": "No pool reserve may be driven to zero by a liquidity removal, and a swap must never pay out more than the constant-product price implies; with x=0 the x*y=k formula degenerates and pays the whole output reserve for one wei.", "locations": [{"raw": "DeFiPlaza.sol:removeLiquidity", "role": "defect"}, {"raw": "DeFiPlaza.sol:swap", "role": "defect"}, {"raw": "DeFiPlaza.sol:addMultiple", "role": "entry_point"}], "explains_findings": [], "valid_findings": [], "invalid_findings": [], "victim_has_source": true, "confidence": "medium", "notes": "The attacker used flash-loaned capital to own almost all LP via addMultiple, then removeLiquidity for ETH: (1-R)^16 in 0.64 fixed point rounds to exactly zero, so the pool pays out its entire ETH balance and the reserve becomes 0; swap() then computes netInput*outBal/((0<<64)+netInput) = the whole output reserve for a 1-wei input, and chaining 1-wei swaps drained every token. This is derived from the recovered code and the PoC call sequence rather than a confirmed post-mortem, hence medium confidence. Slither failed to compile the DeFiPlaza candidate (absolute source path), so there are zero findings to adjudicate."}
{"incident_id": "20240724_Spectrafinance", "reviewer": "fable-5.1 (blind LLM review)", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-22T12:57:23Z", "victim_addresses": ["0x3d20601ac0ba9cae4564ddf7870825c505b69f1a"], "in_scope": true, "off_chain_reason": null, "root_cause": ["input_validation", "arbitrary_external_call"], "mechanism": ["crafted_calldata"], "impact": ["funds_drained"], "violated_invariant": "A router that users approve must restrict which targets/selectors a command may call so a caller cannot make it invoke token.transferFrom on another user's allowance.", "locations": [{"raw": "AMTransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol:_fallback", "role": "entry_point"}], "explains_findings": [], "valid_findings": [], "invalid_findings": [], "victim_has_source": false, "confidence": "high", "notes": "The PoC calls the Spectra router's execute(commands, inputs) with command 0x12 whose input encodes target=asdCRV and calldata transferFrom(victim, attacker, balance); the router executes it with its own approval from the victim, so the defect is an unvalidated external call in the router implementation. Only the proxy/admin source was recovered (implementation missing), so the defect function is absent from the Slither set and the recovered findings are OpenZeppelin proxy noise."}
