te": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 39}, {"candidate": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 40}, {"candidate": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 41}, {"candidate": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 42}, {"candidate": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 43}, {"candidate": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 44}, {"candidate": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 45}, {"candidate": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 46}, {"candidate": "0x7d48d6d775fada207291b37e3eaa68cc865bf9eb", "detector_index": 65}], "victim_has_source": true, "confidence": "high", "notes": "depositFromPairedLpToken is public and takes _slippageOverride with no upper bound; the attacker flash-swapped pOHM, skewed the pOHM/PEAS V3 pool, called it with slippage 999 so amountOutMinimum was ~0.1% of the TWAP quote, and the contract dumped its pOHM into the manipulated pool before the attacker swapped back. Slither's hits on this function (divide-before-multiply, reentrancy-no-eth, unused-return) describe other patterns in the same body, not the unbounded slippage or the manipulable execution price, so none explain the exploit; the uninitialized-local on _adminAmt is a deliberate zero default."}
{"incident_id": "20250407_AmpKashi", "reviewer": "fable-5.1 (blind LLM review)", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-22T12:57:23Z", "victim_addresses": ["0x63d4026cbc902e538618b9aa51a4d05ef48ef5a4"], "in_scope": true, "off_chain_reason": null, "root_cause": ["price_oracle_trust"], "mechanism": ["flash_loan", "price_manipulation"], "impact": ["funds_drained"], "violated_invariant": "Collateral used to back a borrow must be valued by a price that cannot be moved within the same transaction by the borrower.", "locations": [{"raw": "(unrecovered Kashi pair clone):borrow", "role": "entry_point"}, {"raw": "(unrecovered Kashi pair clone):_isSolvent", "role": "defect"}], "explains_findings": [], "valid_findings": [], "invalid_findings": [{"candidate": "0xf5bce5077908a1b7370b9ae04adc565ebd643966", "detector_index": 0}], "victim_has_source": false, "confidence": "low", "notes": "The PoC flash-borrows WETH, pumps AMP across three pools, posts the AMP as Kashi collateral and borrows USDC in the same transaction, which is only possible if the pair's solvency check used an oracle that reflected the pumped price. The Kashi pair clone and its oracle were not recovered, so the defect code is not in the Slither set; BentoBox is only the share vault. The arbitrary-send-erc20 hit on BentoBoxV1.deposit is a false positive because deposit() is gated by the allowed() master-contract approval check."}
{"incident_id": "20250705_ActivePoolScrvUsd", "reviewer": "fable-5.1 (blind LLM review)", "reviewed_at": "2026-10-22T12:57:23Z", "victim_addresses": ["0xd7954a8c7fa74c97ad2545719ce82eae915d73f7"], "in_scope": false, "off_chain_reason": "designed_protocol_behavior: Liquity-v2 urgentRedemption on a shut-down branch pays redeemers a collateral bonus by design; the $4.2k is that bonus captured with flash-loaned USDaf, not a code defect", "root_cause": ["other"], "mechanism": ["flash_loan", "other"], "impact": ["other"], "violated_invariant": "None at the code level: after branch shutdown any USDaf holder is intended to be able to redeem debt for collateral at a small premium so the branch winds down.", "locations": [{"raw": "ActivePool.sol:sendColl", "role": "affected"}], "explains_findings": [], "valid_findings": [], "invalid_findings": [{"candidate": "0xd7954a8c7fa74c97ad2545719ce82eae915d73f7", "detector_index": 196}, {"candidate": "0xd7954a8c7fa74c97ad2545719ce82eae915d73f7", "detector_index": 197}, {"candidate": "0xd7954a8c7fa74c97ad2545719ce82eae915d73f7", "detector_index": 198}], "victim_has_source": true, "confidence": "medium", "notes": "The PoC mints USDaf from flash-loaned USDT and calls TroveManager.urgentRedemption on two chosen troves of the shut-down scrvUSD branch, taking collateral with the protocol's intended redemption bonus; the ActivePool only releases collateral on the TroveManager's instruction. This is designed wind-down behavior rather than a bug, so I mark it out of scope (medium confidence: if the shutdown itself was triggered by a faulty price feed that would be a separate defect in a contract not among the candidates). The reentrancy-no-eth hits in ActivePool are mint calls to the trusted BOLD token and are false positives; nothing explains an exploit here."}
